  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Controlling the spread of the Zika virus in the Caribbean</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To provide funding through the Pan-American Health Organisation (PAHO) to help control the spread of Zika in 8 Caribbean countries (Antigua &amp; Barbuda, Belize, Dominica, Grenada, Guyana, Jamaica, St Lucia and St Vincent and the Grenadines) and the UK overseas territory of Montserrat. The main activities are: procuring pesticides/larvicides and undertaking targeted vector control to reduce mosquito numbers; Information, Education and Communication (IEC) on Zika to help change behaviour; improved surveillance capacity and support for laboratory capacity at the Caribbean Public Health Agency (CARPHA).</narrative>
  </description>
